# decisions.md conflicts on EVERY parallel session, and it never had to.
#
# It is an append only log. Two sessions on the same day both add an entry at
# the end of the file, git sees two different additions starting on the same
# line, and calls it a conflict. It is not one: CLAUDE.md already states the
# resolution, "decisions.md is append only; on conflict keep both entries", and
# every resolution any session has ever made has been exactly that.
#
# `merge=union` is git's built in driver for this. On a conflicting hunk it
# keeps BOTH sides rather than stopping, which is the documented policy applied
# automatically. It cost three hand resolutions on 14 and 15 August alone, and
# on 13 August two sessions' commits were lost to a force push that started as
# a decisions.md conflict.
#
# Union is only safe for a file where two additions never need reconciling, and
# a dated append only log is the textbook case. It is deliberately NOT applied
# to anything else: for code, a silent both-sides merge would be a disaster, so
# every source file keeps the normal driver and its honest conflict.
#
# The order of the two entries after a union merge is not guaranteed to be
# chronological, and that does not matter: every entry carries its own date in
# its heading, which is what anybody reading the file goes by.
plans/decisions.md merge=union
